WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:08.366
The Dormouse came and sat next to Alice.

2
00:00:08.367 --> 00:00:13.801
As Alice began to grow, she thought she should leave the courtroom.

3
00:00:13.802 --> 00:00:16.841
But she was curious about the trial.

4
00:00:16.842 --> 00:00:22.580
So she decided to stay for as long as there was room for her.

5
00:00:22.581 --> 00:00:29.208
"I wish you wouldn't squeeze me like that," the Dormouse complained to Alice.

6
00:00:29.209 --> 00:00:32.925
"I can hardly breathe," the Gryphon said.

7
00:00:32.926 --> 00:00:38.782
"I can't help it," Alice said. "I'm growing."

8
00:00:38.783 --> 00:00:45.348
"Well, you have no right to grow here!" the Dormouse said.

9
00:00:45.349 --> 00:00:50.181
His comment annoyed Alice. "Don't talk nonsense.

10
00:00:50.182 --> 00:00:53.464
You know that you're growing too," she said.

11
00:00:53.465 --> 00:00:59.175
"Yes, but he doesn't do it all at once," the Gryphon said.

12
00:00:59.176 --> 00:01:08.572
The Dormouse and he got up and sat on the other side of the courtroom.

13
00:01:08.573 --> 00:01:12.198
Meanwhile the Queen kept staring at the Hatter.

14
00:01:12.199 --> 00:01:15.439
She waved to one of the soldiers.

15
00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:21.091
"Bring me the list of the singers in the last concert," she said.

16
00:01:21.092 --> 00:01:26.025
When the Hatter heard this, he started to shake again.

17
00:01:26.026 --> 00:01:32.347
"Tell us your story right now," the King said angrily.

18
00:01:32.348 --> 00:01:36.868
"Or I'll have you put to death."

19
00:01:36.869 --> 00:01:41.067
"I'm a poor man, Your Majesty."

20
00:01:41.068 --> 00:01:44.005
The Hatter spoke in a shaky voice.

21
00:01:44.006 --> 00:01:50.761
"I'd just sat down for tea. And then there was the twinkling of tea and—"

22
00:01:50.762 --> 00:01:56.209
"The twinkling of what?" the King asked.

23
00:01:56.210 --> 00:02:01.145
"It began with the tea," the Hatter replied.

24
00:02:01.146 --> 00:02:09.003
"Of course, the word twinkling begins with a T . I'm not

25
00:02:09.004 --> 00:02:18.267
stupid!" The King was growing more impatient every moment. "Go on with your

26
00:02:18.268 --> 00:02:23.268
story." "After the tea twinkled, the March Hare

27
00:02:23.269 --> 00:02:27.024
said—" "I didn't!" the March Hare

28
00:02:27.025 --> 00:02:30.011
interrupted. "You did!" the Hatter

29
00:02:30.012 --> 00:02:33.853
insisted. "I deny it!" the March Hare

30
00:02:33.854 --> 00:02:37.724
said. "He denies it," the King said to the

31
00:02:37.725 --> 00:02:45.614
Hatter. "Leave out the March Hare and continue your

32
00:02:45.615 --> 00:02:48.255
story." Alice looked at the jury

33
00:02:48.256 --> 00:02:58.969
box. All the jurors crossed out "I deny it" on their

34
00:02:58.970 --> 00:03:04.808
slates. "Those two guinea pigs have made a real mess of their slates," she

35
00:03:04.809 --> 00:03:07.737
thought. "Well, then the Dormouse said . . ."

36
00:03:07.738 --> 00:03:13.347
The Hatter looked anxiously at the Dormouse, expecting him to deny everything too.

37
00:03:13.348 --> 00:03:17.900
But the Dormouse was fast asleep.

38
00:03:17.901 --> 00:03:22.954
"After that," the Hatter said, "I had more bread and butter."

39
00:03:22.955 --> 00:03:27.970
"But what did the Dormouse say?" one guinea pig asked.

40
00:03:27.971 --> 00:03:31.740
"I really can't remember," the Hatter said.

41
00:03:31.741 --> 00:03:38.484
"You must remember, or you'll be put to death," the King said.

42
00:03:38.485 --> 00:03:42.014
The Hatter dropped his teacup and his bread and butter.

43
00:03:42.015 --> 00:03:45.591
He went down on one knee in front of the King.

44
00:03:45.592 --> 00:03:51.121
"I'm a poor man, Your Majesty," he repeated.

45
00:03:51.122 --> 00:03:56.350
"You're a very poor speaker," the King said.

46
00:03:56.351 --> 00:04:01.392
"Woo-hoo!" Here the second guinea pig cheered.

47
00:04:01.393 --> 00:04:05.588
A soldier immediately took it away.

48
00:04:05.589 --> 00:04:12.380
"If that's all you know, you may leave," the King said to the Hatter.

49
00:04:12.381 --> 00:04:20.630
And here the other guinea pig cheered and was removed from the jury box.

50
00:04:20.631 --> 00:04:24.884
"I'd rather finish my tea first," the Hatter said.

51
00:04:24.885 --> 00:04:30.540
He shot a quick look at the Queen, who was reading the list of singers.

52
00:04:30.541 --> 00:04:34.490
"You may go," the King said.

53
00:04:34.491 --> 00:04:38.483
The Hatter rushed from the courtroom.

54
00:04:38.484 --> 00:04:45.852
"Just take his head off outside," the Queen said to one of the soldiers.

55
00:04:45.853 --> 00:04:51.346
But the Hatter was out of sight before the soldier got to the doors.

56
00:04:51.347 --> 00:04:54.558
Alice shook her head in disbelief.

57
00:04:54.559 --> 00:04:56.929
"The Hatter wasn't any help at all.

58
00:04:56.930 --> 00:05:02.200
At this rate, we'll never find out if the Knave of Hearts is guilty," she thought.

59
00:05:02.201 --> 00:05:07.372
"Call the next witness!" the King said.

